On Dec 5, 6:23 am, "sjdevn...@yahoo.com" <sjdevn...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> On Dec 4, 9:02 pm, Cuboidz <Dieter.Be...@gmail.com> wrote:

> > I'm pretty new to Nethack, and I've come to dislike shops because of
> > all the drudgery involved in putting them to good use: price-ID'ing
> > scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...

> > So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> > only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> > encounter a shop?

> I price-ID scrolls until I have identify, enchant armor/remove curse,
> and enchant weapon.  I'll price-ID lamps too (for magic).

I tend to make a more ad hoc decision.  I'll generally price-id
anything I have on me: that's fairly fast, and very accurate
(charisma doesn't place a role).  I'll also generally ask the
price of all of the objects, just in case one or the other might
be immediately identifiable this way: the scrolls you mention,
and the lamp, but also a very expensive wand, etc.  Also
anything that might be magic armor.  Beyond that, it depends on
my needs and my feeling: I might look for rings or potions at
300, for example, or I might come back and do that later.

Same thing for stealing.  If I've got a pet handy, and something
in the shop looks particularly interesting, or I have a lot of
tripe (to get it trained quickly), I might hang around; most of
the time, however, I don't bother.

> Otherwise I just buy what I need, unless I've lucked into a
> magic whistle or something and there's something that's really
> worth the effort.  Early on I may spend a bit more effort if
> it'll get me magic resistance or something like that, but
> usually it's easier just to get the money and buy it.

Early on, the money is best spent for protection (and except for
tools, most of the things you might really want are expensive.
Later on, of course, money is no problem.

I'll also try and keep at least one general shopkeeper alive
just in case I want to price id later.  If I'm short on scrolls
of id, for example, I'll price id rings before using them, to be
sure that I get the identity on the ones costing 200 or 300.  (I
generally don't kill them myself, but if I have a decent pet,
I'll single out one shop, and keep the pet out of it.)

